<title>INDIA: India 96/97 coffee output seen at 220,000 tonnes.</title>
<headline>India 96/97 coffee output seen at 220,000 tonnes.</headline>
<dateline>NEW DELHI 1997-02-25</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Indian government said on Tuesday that the country is expected to produce 220,000 tonnes of coffee in 1996/97 (July-June), down slightly from 223,000 in the previous year.</p>
<p>The government said in its annual Economic Survey that 113,000 tonnes of coffee was exported between April 1 and November 15, 1996.</p>
<p>India exported 170,000 tonnes of coffee in fiscal 1995/96 (April-March), about 76 percent of the the year's output.</p>
<p>-- New Delhi newsroom +91-11 301 2024</p>
</text>
